load @/code/structure/set
  find set

# The boundary at infinity: the set of ideal points a hyperbolic space approaches but never reaches, the rim of the
# Poincare disk, the horizon. Geodesics run out to ideal points, and the boundary carries its own geometry (a sphere one
# dimension down) on which the space's symmetries act. In the substrate this ideal boundary is the thin skin of the
# baseball, the cusp where the bulk meets physical reality. The form carries the set of ideal points.
form ideal-boundary
  link points, like set
